    "title": "Rapper Offset, Cardi B’s ex-husband, shot near South Florida casino",
    "text": "by Gershon HarrellMon, April 6, 2026 at 11:09 PMUpdated Tue, April 7, 2026 at 6:30 AMFILE - Offset arrives at the iHeartRadio Music Awards, March 17, 2025, at the Dolby Theatre in Los Angeles. (Photo by Jordan Strauss/Invision/AP, File)HOLLWOOD, Fla. (CBS12) — Rapper Offset, the ex-husband of Cardi B, was shot in Florida on Monday, according to multiple reports.According to CBS Miami, the Migos rapper was shot near the Seminole Hard Rock Hotel & Casino in Hollywood. He was taken to a hospital in stable condition with non-life-threatening injuries.\"We can confirm Offset was shot and is currently at the hospital receiving medical care,\" his representative told Variety. \"He is stable and being closely monitored.\"See also: Deputies rescue Florida woman trapped in submerged car after crash into retention pondCBS Miami says authorities have not released details about what led to the shooting.Rapper Offset, Cardi B’s ex-husband, shot near South Florida casinoFILE - Cardi B, left, and Offset arrive at the Pre-Grammy Gala And Salute To Industry Icons in Beverly Hills, Calif. on Jan. 25, 2020. (Photo by Mark Von Holden/Invision/AP, File)As of Monday night, the shooting remains under investigation, CBS Miami says.The incident comes more than three years after Takeoff, who was part of Migos with Offset, was shot and killed in Houston.Rapper Offset, the ex-husband of Cardi B, was shot in Florida on Monday, according to multiple reports. According to TMZ, the Migos rapper was shot near the Seminole Hard Rock Hotel & Casino in Hollywood. He was taken to a hospital in stable condition with non-life-threatening injuries. (Reuters){ }The Grammy-nominated rap trio formed in 2008 in Georgia. They released their first major hit, “Versace,” in 2013 and rose to the top of the charts in 2016 with “Bad and Boujee,” featuring Lil Uzi Vert.",
